import FocusDeals from './lib/FocusDeals.abide'
import focusDeals from './lib/FocusDeals.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import RankDeals from './lib/RankDeals.abide'
import rankDeals from './lib/RankDeals.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/headless/announce', '/headless/sortable-table']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/DealPriorities.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the deals selected move together with Alt and the arrows'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/sortableList.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a grip dragged places its item among the others by the pointer",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/DealFocus.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('Alt with ArrowLeft and ArrowRight moves a deal between this week and later'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/sortableList.test.ts',
            from: [
                'test("a grip dragged into another list of its group moves its item there',
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Rank deals by dragging or with the keys">
        <p>A sortable list is a <code>listbox</code>. Spread <code>list</code> on the list and
            <code>item(entry).item</code> on each item. It is one stop in the tab order: the
            arrows, Home and End move what is active, and a click, a ⌘ or Ctrl click and a Shift
            click select as in any listbox. Alt with ArrowUp or ArrowDown moves the item a place,
            or the whole selection where the item is in it. Spread <code>.handle</code> on a grip
            to drag them; it is for the pointer alone, hidden from the keyboard. Each move is
            read out through <code>announce</code>, so stand an <code>announce.host</code> on
            the page.</p>
        <Example code={rankDeals}><RankDeals /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Move deals between this week and later">
        <p>Give two lists the same <code>group</code> and each takes the other's items. Drag a
            grip onto the other list, or press Alt with ArrowLeft or ArrowRight to send the item
            to the list before or after it; focus goes with it. Each list's <code>order</code> is
            written on the move, and the announcement names the list by its
            <code>aria-label</code>. Give an empty list a height, so a drag has somewhere to
            land.</p>
        <Example code={focusDeals}><FocusDeals /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
